    retrieval_eligible: true,
    rag_text: 'Title: NDPS Act, 1985 — Section 37 Offences to be Cognizable and Non-Bailable (Twin Conditions for Bail)\nSection: Section 37\nAct: NDPS Act, 1985\nChapter: Chapter IV - Offences and Penalties\nQuestion: What are the twin conditions for granting bail under Section 37 of the NDPS Act, 1985?\nAnswer: Under Section 37, all NDPS offences are cognizable. For offences under Section 19, 24, 27A, and all commercial quantity offences, bail cannot be granted unless the Public Prosecutor has an opportunity to oppose, and the court is satisfied there are reasonable grounds for believing the accused is not guilty and is not likely to commit any offence while on bail.'
