    answer: 'Section 52 of the NDPS Act, 1985 prescribes the initial statutory custody and forwarding procedures upon arrest and seizure:\n\n1. **Informing Grounds of Arrest (Section 52(1))**:\n   * Any officer arresting a person under Section 41, Section 42, Section 43 or Section 44 shall, **as soon may be, inform him of the full grounds for such arrest** (fulfilling Article 22(1) of the Constitution).\n\n2. **Disposal under Warrant (Section 52(2))**:\n   * Every person arrested and article seized under a warrant issued under sub-section (1) of Section 41 shall be forwarded without unnecessary delay to the Magistrate by whom the warrant was issued.\n\n3. **Disposal without Warrant (Section 52(3))**:\n   * Every person arrested and article seized under Section 41(2), Section 42, Section 43 or Section 44 shall be forwarded without unnecessary delay to:\n     * (a) The **officer-in-charge of the nearest police station**; or\n     * (b) The **officer empowered under Section 53** (investigating officer invested with police station in-charge powers).\n\n4. **Duty of Receiving Officer (Section 52(4))**:\n   * The officer receiving the custody of arrested persons and seized articles must take immediate steps to produce them before a Magistrate and take custody of articles in the police station malkhana.',
