    answer: 'Section 68A of the NDPS Act, 1985 defines the categories of persons subject to Chapter VA forfeiture:\n\n1. **Convicted Persons (Section 68A(2)(a))**:\n   * Every person who has been convicted of an offence punishable under the NDPS Act with imprisonment for a term of **ten years or more**.\n\n2. **Preventive Detenus under PIT NDPS Act (Section 68A(2)(b))**:\n   * Every person in respect of whom an order of detention has been made under the Prevention of Illicit Traffic in Narcotic Drugs and Psychotropic Substances Act, 1988 (PIT NDPS Act) or Jammu and Kashmir Prevention of Illicit Traffic in Narcotic Drugs and Psychotropic Substances Act, 1988:\n   * Provided that such order of detention has not been revoked on the report of the Advisory Board or set aside by a court of competent jurisdiction.\n\n3. **Relatives and Associates (Section 68A(2)(c) & (d))**:\n   * Every person who is a **relative** (spouse, siblings, lineal ascendants, lineal descendants, and spouses of siblings/descendants) of a person referred to in clause (a) or clause (b);\n   * Every **associate** (business partner, employer, employee, agent, trustee, or company where 20% or more voting power is held);\n   * Any holder of any property which was at any time previously held by a person referred to in clause (a) or (b) unless acquired for adequate consideration in good faith.',
