    retrieval_eligible: true,
    rag_text: 'Title: NDPS Rules, 1985 — Framework for Regulated Manufacture, Possession, Transport, and Licences\nSection: NDPS Rules, 1985\nAct: NDPS Rules, 1985\nChapter: Chapters III to VI - Cultivation, Manufacture, and Licencing\nQuestion: What is the regulatory framework under the NDPS Rules, 1985 for legal manufacture, transport, and import/export of narcotic drugs and psychotropic substances?\nAnswer: The NDPS Rules, 1985 govern lawful medical and scientific operations, licensing of opium poppy cultivation by the Central Bureau of Narcotics, Government Opium Factories (Ghazipur/Neemuch), pharmaceutical manufacturing quotas, and import/export authorizations.'
