    question: 'What are the mandatory sampling quantities, storage guidelines, and test memo procedures under the NDPS Seizure, Storage, Sampling and Disposal Rules, 2022?',
    answer: 'The Narcotic Drugs and Psychotropic Substances (Seizure, Storage, Sampling and Disposal) Rules, 2022 (notified vide G.S.R. 899(E) dated 23.12.2022) establish strict standard operating procedures under Section 52A of the Act:\n\n1. **Sampling Quantity Standards (Rule 10)**:\n   * For **Opium, Ganja, and Charas (cannabis resin)**: Samples must be drawn in **duplicate**, each sample weighing not less than **24 grams**.\n   * For **all other narcotic drugs and psychotropic substances** (including Heroin, Cocaine, MDMA, Amphetamine, Psychotropic Tablets): Samples must be drawn in **duplicate**, each sample weighing not less than **5 grams**.\n\n2. **Magisterial Supervision (Rule 8 & 9)**:\n   * Drawing of representative samples MUST be conducted before the Magistrate upon an application filed under Section 52A(2). Spot sampling at the site of recovery is superseded by the magisterial procedure.\n\n3. **Test Memo and Dispatch to Forensic Laboratory (Rule 11)**:\n   * Samples must be dispatched to the designated Forensic Science Laboratory (FSL/CRCL) accompanied by **Test Memo in Form 6** within **seventy-two hours (72 hours)** of drawing samples before the Magistrate.\n\n4. **Storage in Malkhana (Rule 6 & 7)**:\n   * Case property must be stored in a dedicated strong room or Malkhana inside a **double-lock trunk/safe** with separate keys kept by the Malkhana In-Charge and the Gazetted Supervisory Officer, subject to mandatory bi-monthly inspections.',
